{"id":"c3ce21cf-9bc8-4524-8017-b3872eaf1d92","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.012","title":"Cross-species multiomic atlas of the primate basal ganglia","title_zh":"灵长类动物基底神经节跨物种多组学图谱","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.012","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.012","abstract":"The basal ganglia (BG) are conserved brain regions essential for motor control, learning, emotion, and cognition and are implicated in neurological and psychiatric disease, yet a unified cross-species taxonomy of BG cell types is lacking. We present a multiomic consensus atlas of 1.8 million nuclei from humans, macaques, and marmosets spanning eight BG structures, integrating gene expression, open chromatin, and spatial profiling. Alignment across species and to mouse and human whole-brain atlases identifies 61 homologous cell types conserved over 76 million years. Dorsal-ventral spatial identity is more conserved than D1/D2 receptor or striosome/matrix identity, and striatum (STR) D2 SMYD2-HTR7 spiny projection neurons have distinct molecular, electrophysiological, and morphological features. Cis-regulatory analysis reveals conserved sequence grammars that encode cell identity and inform viral targeting, and cell-type-resolved mapping localizes psychiatric and neurodegenerative risk to specific BG cell populations. This work provides a foundational resource for BG evolution, function, and disease.","abstract_zh":"基底神经节（BG）是保守的脑区，对运动控制、学习、情绪和认知至关重要，并与神经系统和精神疾病相关，但迄今尚缺乏统一的跨物种基底神经节细胞类型分类体系。本研究构建了人、猕猴和狨猴八个基底神经节结构中180万个细胞核的多组学共识图谱，整合了基因表达、开放染色质和空间定性数据。跨物种对齐并与小鼠和人全脑图谱比对，鉴定出在7600万年进化过程中保守的61种同源细胞类型。背侧-腹侧空间身份比D1/D2受体或条状体/基质身份更具保守性；纹状体（STR）D2 SMYD2-HTR7棘状投射神经元具有独特的分子、电生理和形态学特征。顺式调控分析揭示了编码细胞身份并为病毒靶向提供依据的保守序列语法，细胞类型分辨的图谱将精神疾病和神经退行性疾病风险定位到特定的基底神经节细胞群体。该工作为基底神经节的进化、功能和疾病研究提供了基础资源。","snippet":"The basal ganglia (BG) are conserved brain regions essential for motor control, learning, emotion, and cognition and are implicated in neurological and psychiatric disease, yet a unified cross-species taxonomy of BG cell types is lacking. We present a multiomic consensus atlas of 1.8 million nuclei from humans, macaques, and marmosets spanning eight BG structures, integrating gene expression, open chromatin, and spa…","translated_at":"2026-11-14T08:11:26.352478Z","translation_model":"nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":"189","issue":"23","published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-11-12T23:34:37Z","display_date":"2026-11-12T23:34:37Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Nelson J. Johansen","authors_text":"Nelson J. Johansen, Yuanyuan Fu, Matthew Schmitz, Alma Dubuc, Niklas Kempynck, Morgan Wirthlin, Aaron D. Garcia, Madeleine Hewitt, Meghan A. Turner, Stephanie C. Seeman, Brian Long, Xiao-Ping Liu, Agata Budzillo, Shu Dan, Michael DeBerardine, Inkar Kapen, Anna Marie Yanny, Wubin Ding, Alida Avola, Samuel T. Barlow, Darren Bertagnolli, Ashwin Bhandiwad, Victor Eduardo Nieto Caballero, Lakme Caceres, Tamara Casper, Anish Bhaswanth Chakka, Rushil Chakrabarty, Michael Clark, Scott Daniel, Jeroen Eggermont, Rebecca Ferrer, Leon French, Jessica Gloe, Jeff Goldy, Nathan Guilford, Junitta Guzman, Daniel Hirschstein, Windy Ho, Katelyn James, Danielle Lynne Jones, Matthew Jungert, Madhav Kannan, Kasia Z. Kedzierska, Thomas Kroes, Mckaila Leytze, Arena Manning, Rachel McCue, Chris Morrison, Beagan Nguy, Sven Otto, Nick Pena, Trangthanh Pham, Elliot Phillips, Abhejit Rajagopal, Christine Rimorin, Andrea D. Rivera, Dana Rocha, Raymond Sanchez, Geoffrey Schau, Jessica Schembri, Nadiya V. Shapovalova, Jamie Sherman, Julian Thijssen, Michael Tieu, Amy Torkelson, Alex Tran, Alexander Vieth, Yongqi Wang, Dan Yuan, Jennie Close, Tanya L. Daigle, Rachel Dalley, Nick Dee, Song-Lin Ding, Elysha Fiabane, Nathan Gouwens, Grace Huynh, Brian R. Lee, Boaz P. Levi, Delissa McMillen, Jeremy A. Miller, Tyler Mollenkopf, Lydia Ng, 